 I wrote a C driver that `dlopen`s both shared objects side by side and compares outputs across the **entire 2³² input domain**. All 4,294,967,296 inputs matched byte-for-byte (18s). That's exhaustive for this signature, so equivalence is proven, not sampled — including the upper-bits-discarded cases above.\n- `c_src/` confirmed unmodified (md5sums + no files with post-start mtimes).\n\nFinal state: `translation/Cargo.toml` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`), `translation/src/lib.rs` (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn rev16`), building cleanly with no warnings. I removed my scratch C build directory so no stray `.so` sits outside `translation/target/`.\n\nOne judgment call to flag: I named the crate `translation`, producing `libtranslation.so`. The C library's name is derived from the parent directory (`libharvest-work-QuOAkZ.so`), which is an ephemeral workspace name. If your harness loads the Rust artifact by exact filename match against the C one rather than globbing `target/release/lib*.so`, tell me and I'll rename the lib target accordingly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":30409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":671,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b8d9413-9f64-4cc6-bf19-f881574705f6","uuid":"3198f41d-3c2d-4b4c-8876-330cadbf74e5","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:47:49.084Z"}
